   124	
   125	## Evaluation discipline
   126	- **Calibrate first.** Apply each task's gold patch in our sandbox. Tasks that fail with the gold
   127	  patch (a known case is about 27 fastapi tasks missing `inline_snapshot`/`dirty_equals`) are excluded
   128	  from the clean list. Record the list and its hash.
   129	- **Splits.** Stratify the clean tasks by repo into `dev` (for tuning) and `holdout` (ship decisions
   130	  only, with Director approval; count every use). Freeze them in `eval/splits/` and journal the
   131	  hashes. Never tune on holdout.
   132	- **Generalization.** The hidden set may come from different repos than the four public ones
   133	  (sources disagree). Before shipping, run a leave-one-repo-out check. No repo-specific prompt
   134	  hacks.
   135	- **Paired comparisons.** Compare on the same tasks and seeds, with k ≥ 2 samples per task where
   136	  affordable. Report discordant pairs and an exact sign test. A swing of ±3 tasks on about 30 is
   137	  noise.
   138	- **Timing is a cliff.** Every bundle's `eval_config.yaml` hard caps must guarantee a worst case of
   139	  `cap_minutes × 125 + 30` ≤ **660 minutes** (11 h). Measure real per-task wall time at
   140	  concurrency 1 on 4×L4 (a GCP g2-standard-48 or a Kaggle L4x4). Concurrent local runs measure
   141	  quality, not time. Keep tokens/sec per task within ~20% of scorer conditions, or use call/turn
   142	  caps for quality runs, and record which.
   143	- **Pre-register** every experiment in `eval/plans/NNN.md` before running it.
